      "math_academy_id": "e-13015",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\sqrt{\\dfrac{9}{64}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $a\\geq 0,$ then \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{a^2} = a.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $9$ and $64$ are both perfect squares, where\n\n$$\n9=3^2,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n64 = 8^2.\n$$\n\nSo, to work out $\\sqrt{\\dfrac{9}{64}},$ we express $\\dfrac{9}{64}$ as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{64}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{8}^{2}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{3\\cdot 3}{8\\cdot 8}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{8})}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{8} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151336/observations/step-e13015-9075436f4b6d5566ae2f.html",
